  "notes": "USAGE:\nSense 1 is used in political and international law contexts, especially in the phrase {民族|みんぞく}{自決|じけつ} (national self-determination). Sense 2 is a euphemistic term encountered primarily in historical and military writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {民族|みんぞく}{自決|じけつ} (national self-determination)\n- {自決|じけつ}する (to determine for oneself; to take one's own life)\n- {自決|じけつ}を{図|はか}る (to attempt suicide)\n- {自決|じけつ}の{権利|けんり} (right to self-determination)",
